general_comments.body:
@NickolasBenakis Sorry about that, the PR changed a bit.
To replace `mode: 'above`, you need to write something like
```
fill: {
  target: 'origin',
  above: yourColor,
  below: 'transparent'
}
```

@kurkle I have been doing a few benchmarks using Chromium, Firefox and JSBench.me.
Seems like the difference is insignificant when creating charts with 1000 values with gaps (< 1%)

<details><summary>Just to illustrate the kind of Chart I use in my benchmarks :</summary>
<p>

```javascript
var lineData = [];
var curveData = [];
var labels = [];
for (var i = 0 ; i < 1000 ; i++) {
  curveData.push(Math.floor(Math.random() * 5));
  lineData.push(3);
  labels.push('' + i);
}


var chartData = {
  labels: labels,
  datasets: [{
    fill: '+1',
    tension: 0.5,
    data: curveData,
    borderColor: '#0000AA',
    borderWidth: 2,
  },
  {
    type: 'line',
    fill: "false",
    tension: 0,
    data: lineData,
    borderColor: "#00ADEE",
    borderWidth: 2,
  }]
};
```

</p>
</details>

