@benmccann I agree it's useful for *reference* but this is *getting started* documentation, which should be more goal-oriented than abstract reference type content.

Also do note that the full list is still included, but in a place where it is better explained and you need to know about it ("How to choose the imports you require").

Final note: inspecting `registerables` (which is suggested in that section too) is possibly a better way to achieve what you're after anyway, since it can be done from the version of the library you're actually using - so you can see in-browser what's there and how ChartJS has chosen to group the classes.

