general_comments.body:
About this PR, could make sense to expose the interactions object in order to enable the user to use a default interpolator in own custom one?

```javascript
const myInterpolator = function(from, to, factor, prop) {
  if (prop === 'something') {
    // my logic
    return myValue;
  }
  // use the default one? as property of "animation" instance
  return this.interpolators.color(from, to, factor, prop);
};
```

Waiting for @kurkle feedback, I think a dedicated PR is needed anyway, to expose the default interpolators. 

This is because more time is also needed to evaluate how `animations.[key].type` and an interpolator are stricly related. In the meanwhile, it's in my TODO.
For instance, I want to interpolate a font options (see sample in chartjs annotation, https://github.com/chartjs/chartjs-plugin-annotation/pull/847) :

```javascript
        animations: {
          fonts: {
            properties: ['font'],
            type: 'font',
            fn(from, to, factor) {
              const f = Object.assign({}, to);
              f.size = f.size * factor;
              return f;
            }
          },
        },
```

I have set `type: 'font',` even if it's a recognized type. And `fn` option is in this way mandatory otherwise there is an error. Maybe the interpolators should be extendable with custom type.

